        <register>
          <name>TIM_CCR7</name>
          <displayName>TIM_CCR7</displayName>
          <description>TIM capture/compare register 7</description>
          <addressOffset>0x070</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>CCR7</name>
              <description>Capture/compare 7 value</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>20</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>TIM_CCMR4</name>
          <displayName>TIM_CCMR4</displayName>
          <description>TIM capture/compare mode register 4</description>
          <addressOffset>0x078</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>OC7FE</name>
              <description>Output compare 7 fast enable</description>
              <bitOffset>2</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>CC7 behaves normally depending on counter and CCR7 values even when the trigger is ON. The minimum delay to activate CC7 output when an edge occurs on the trigger input is 5 clock cycles.</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>An active edge on the trigger input acts like a compare match on CC7 output. Then, OC is set to the compare level independently from the result of the comparison. Delay to sample the trigger input and to activate CC7 output is reduced to 3 clock cycles. OCFE acts only if the channel is configured in PWM1 or PWM2 mode.</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>OC7PE</name>
              <description>Output compare 7 preload enable</description>
              <bitOffset>3</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>Preload register on TIMx_CCR7 disabled. TIMx_CCR7 can be written at anytime, the new value is taken in account immediately.</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>Preload register on TIMx_CCR7 enabled. Read/Write operations access the preload register. TIMx_CCR7 preload value is loaded in the active register at each update event.</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>OC7M</name>
              <description>OC7M[2:0]: Output compare 7 mode</description>
              <bitOffset>4</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>3</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>Frozen - The comparison between the output compare register TIMx_CCR7 and the counter TIMx_CNT has no effect on the outputs.(this mode is used to generate a timing base).</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>Set channel 7 to active level on match. tim_oc7ref signal is forced high when the counter TIMx_CNT matches the capture/compare register 7 (TIMx_CCR7).</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x2</name>
                  <description>Set channel 7 to inactive level on match. tim_oc7ref signal is forced low when the counter TIMx_CNT matches the capture/compare register 7 (TIMx_CCR7).</description>
                  <value>0x2</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x3</name>
                  <description>Toggle - tim_oc7ref toggles when TIMx_CNT = TIMx_CCR7.</description>
                  <value>0x3</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x4</name>
                  <description>Force inactive level - tim_oc7ref is forced low.</description>
                  <value>0x4</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x5</name>
                  <description>Force active level - tim_oc7ref is forced high.</description>
                  <value>0x5</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x6</name>
                  <description>PWM mode 1 - In upcounting, channel 7 is active as long as TIMx_CNTless thanTIMx_CCR7 else inactive. In downcounting, channel 7 is inactive (tim_oc7ref = 0) as long as TIMx_CNT&gt;TIMx_CCR7 else active (tim_oc5ref = 1).</description>
                  <value>0x6</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x7</name>
                  <description>PWM mode 2 - In upcounting, channel 7 is inactive as long as TIMx_CNTless thanTIMx_CCR7 else active. In downcounting, channel 7 is active as long as TIMx_CNT&gt;TIMx_CCR7 else inactive.</description>
                  <value>0x7</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>OC7CE</name>
              <description>Output compare 7 clear enable</description>
              <bitOffset>7</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>1</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>tim_oc7ref is not affected by the tim_ocref_clr_int signal</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>tim_oc7ref is cleared as soon as a High level is detected on tim_ocref_clr_int signal (tim_ocref_clr input or tim_etrf input)</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
              </enumeratedValues>
            </field>
            <field>
              <name>OC7M_1</name>
              <description>OC7M[4:3]</description>
              <bitOffset>16</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
            </field>
          </fields>
        </register>
        <register>
          <name>TIM_MPR1</name>
          <displayName>TIM_MPR1</displayName>
          <description>TIM multilevel protection register 1</description>
          <addressOffset>0x090</addressOffset>
          <size>0x20</size>
          <access>read-write</access>
          <resetValue>0x00000000</resetValue>
          <resetMask>0xFFFFFFFF</resetMask>
          <fields>
            <field>
              <name>BK1M</name>
              <description>Break mode for tim_oc1 output</description>
              <bitOffset>0</bitOffset>
              <bitWidth>2</bitWidth>
              <access>read-write</access>
              <enumeratedValues>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x0</name>
                  <description>Immediate break</description>
                  <value>0x0</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
                <enumeratedValue>
                  <name>B_0x1</name>
                  <description>Delayed 1 break</description>
                  <value>0x1</value>
                </enumeratedValue>
